// A permit and a forbid over the same predicate (Login) but with
// different windows. Models a realistic "broad allow with narrow
// freshness exclusion" pattern: Read is generally allowed for 2h
// post-login, but the first 30m are blocked (e.g., to wait for
// post-login session setup to settle).
//
// Both rules reference the same predicate, so per-rule sub-plan
// state cannot be safely shared across them — each must keep its
// own `Since` state under its own `pol{j}:opN` SQL prefix.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 2h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};

forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 30m Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
